# Base image for every FROM in infrastructure/docker/Dockerfile: the same Docker Official Image pin the website and the
# Cloud Assessor pair use, python:3.14.8-slim-trixie (CPython 3.14.8 on Debian 13), by index digest. The Dockerfile does not read this file: it repeats the digest in full on each
# FROM line, and nothing in CI compares the two, so this file is documentation and the two must be changed together by hand. The tag beside the
# digest is documentation; Docker resolves the digest. Plain shell assignments, read by /bin/sh.
# Checked on 2026-10-25 with `docker buildx imagetools inspect python:3.14.8-slim-trixie@<digest>`: the digest below still
# resolves to the Docker Official Image index for python:3.14.8-slim-trixie, and the image job builds from it. The tag has
# been rebuilt since the pin was taken (today it points at sha256:fbecd461fc72d21b2143c6eaba25143738079154a6d0ea3da3aec724f50eed4a);
# the pin is not moved here because a new base image is its own reviewed change (the weekly image scan, image-scan.yml,
# and its pull request trigger on this folder exist for that). To move it, resolve the new digest the same way and change
# this file and both FROM lines of the Dockerfile together.
PYTHON_IMAGE=python:3.14.8-slim-trixie
PYTHON_IMAGE_DIGEST=sha256:a2b82f3c48559aa0a8446d9af49826b6e2b2016f4cd2afabfe6013ec53729170
PYTHON_VERSION=3.14.8
